                <pb facs="0234" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10926: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-24T12:00:00+08:00">June 24,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 24—10:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>490. Legation’s 468, June 19, 2 p.m.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d125-f1"/> Following
                    from American Consul at Tsinanfu: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 23, 6 p.m. Han has just informed the Consuls that he will withdraw
                            from Tsinanfu within the next 3 or 4 days east along <pb facs="0235"
                                n="137" xml:id="pg137"/> the Kiaochow Railway since the fall of
                            Changching is imminent. We again expressed the hope that there will be
                            no fighting here and that the local police will be left with arms and
                            ammunition. He promised the latter but said he did not know whether the
                            Shansi forces would permit him to withdraw unmolested or fight a
                            rear-guard action with him to the suburbs of Tsinanfu. Han apparently
                            has no understanding with the other side regarding withdrawal. Would it
                            be possible to request Shansi military authorities to enter Tsinanfu
                            only after the departure of Han’s troops. Nearly all Americans have now
                            left here.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
